{# The capacity check has to run AFTER the invoke, and the skeleton's only
   post-invoke seam in the iteration is this one, so it leads the CSV dump
   rather than sitting between the run and the HPX_ITER header as it did when
   this template stood alone.  The error and the park are unchanged; what
   changed is that the iteration header is already on the wire when they fire,
   which if anything tells the host which iteration overflowed. #}
{% block engine_print_csv %}        if (g_layer_capacity_exceeded) {
