{#- engine_profiled_summary: overridden to (void)-reads only, so this
    engine emits no HPX_PROFILED_INFER_COUNT / _TOTAL_US / _AVG_US at all --
    the same wire surface it had before it became a child.

    nsx::executorch::run_once_profiled() is load + execute, and the base's
    per-pass loop DWT-brackets exactly that call, so the base's default would
    publish load+execute cost under the keys every other engine uses for
    execute-only timing.  Two independent consumers would take it at face
    value: the comparability model treats ComparisonDimension.ENGINE as
    INFORMATIVE (results/dimensions.py -- reported, never blocking; MODEL_SHA256
    is the only identity dimension), so cross-engine comparisons are not gated
    on it; and validation/runner.py falls back to device_profiled_infer_avg_us
    as the run latency, which would silently become "time to load and run".

    The base's profiled_infer_cycles/count accumulation still happens inside the
    loop -- it is a couple of DWT reads per iteration and keeping it in the
    shared path keeps that loop identical for every engine.  Nothing reads the
    result here, so read it explicitly: the base's summary was the only
    consumer, and without these the variables are set-but-unused under -Wall
    in every ExecuTorch render (#161). -#}
{% block engine_profiled_summary %}

    (void)profiled_infer_cycles;
    (void)profiled_infer_count;{% endblock %}
